      "discriminative_explanation": "The observations describe two distinct types of folding. Observation img-k7-o1 describes folds that are 'arranged vertically on one side and cross over the other,' creating a specific asymmetrical pattern. In contrast, observation img-v9-o0 describes 'vertical, parallel folds' that descend from the top. Because the geometric arrangement of the folds differs between the described objects (crossing vs. parallel), the observation that the 'folding is the same operation' is not supported by the visual evidence provided.",
      "unresolved_alternatives": "The claims do not specify which objects are being compared. If the claim refers only to the two objects within the single photograph set (ignoring the different descriptions provided for different images), it might be true, but the text explicitly contrasts the 'crossing' nature of one description with the 'parallel' nature of another, indicating at least two different folding operations are visually present."
